{
	title: 'Optional Pi command extension adapter',
	spec: 'extras/pi-compat.ts supplies an opt-in native plugin adapter for explicitly imported trusted Pi command extensions, verified against unmodified pi-simplify 0.2.3. Support synchronous registerCommand, command descriptions/help/completion through host commands and shared command list, invocation-bound cwd and ui.notify, argv exec with captured output, timeout and cancellation, and sendUserMessage followUp through queued literal Hal prompts with provenance. Unsupported APIs and command collisions fail visibly. Async invocations retain their own session and cwd; unload cancels pending processes and prevents late messages. Commands are available through the existing host paths to terminal and web; simplify completion includes --staged and --ref=. Keep external packages/config explicit and optional, no automatic discovery, downloads, Pi runtime dependency, telemetry or emulation of broader Pi APIs. Document pinned setup and upstream simplify behavior. Retain contract tests for isolation, delivery, collisions, cancellation and cleanup; verify actual published extension against real Git fixtures.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Implemented as an optional extras installer, without core changes or Pi runtime dependencies. Wrapper supplies simplify flag completion because upstream has none. Exec uses argv subprocess groups, a 30000ms default timeout, and owner-scoped abort on turns.stop or unload. Nonzero exits retain code and output and are also shown because upstream otherwise hides Git errors. Only synchronous initialization is supported by the native plugin loader.',
		'Verified the published pi-simplify 0.2.3 entry unchanged against actual Git: two baseline commits (second empty), no-change notice, staged line-2 hunk, explicit file with HEAD~1, busy after-turn delivery, and nonrepository Git diagnostics. Disposable probe passed 14 assertions; durable adapter contracts passed 4 tests and 42 assertions. Adjacent plugins/slash/foreign-hook regression run passed 47 tests. Typecheck and adapter lint passed. Bun AbortError stacks can omit the message, so command errors preserve both message and stack. Session routing, literal escaping and canceled-invocation guards are lasting invariants.',
		'Measured 216 source LOC and 165 test LOC excluding blanks and comments. No timers run while idle and completed invocations leave the active set; persistent adapter state is command registrations only. Upstream launches one hunk subprocess per changed file concurrently, so 10x files means 10x calls. Host command discovery/help/completion paths are covered; no browser rendering changes or browser automation were needed.'
	],
	needs: ['fsg', 'an']
}
